Amethyst: make glfwSetWindowIcon a silent no-op on macOS again.

macOS windows have no icon of their own (the Dock shows the application's icon), so GLFW has
never done anything here on Cocoa. Up to GLFW 3.3 the call returned silently. Upstream commit
9a87c2a4 ("Add feature available/implemented errors", GLFW 3.4 development) made it report
GLFW_FEATURE_UNAVAILABLE (65548), "Cocoa: Regular windows do not have icons on macOS".
LWJGL 3.3.1 is built from that development branch.

Minecraft 1.13 to 1.18 were made for LWJGL 3.1/3.2 (GLFW 3.2/3.3). On an arm64 JVM they run on
LWJGL 3.3.1 instead, the first LWJGL with arm64 macOS natives. They call glfwSetWindowIcon right
after creating the window, while their start-up GLFW error callback still treats any error as
fatal. The game then stops with "GLFW error 65548: Cocoa: Regular windows do not have icons on
macOS" and never opens a window.

The argument checks in glfwSetWindowIcon (window.c) are unchanged.

--- a/src/cocoa_window.m
+++ b/src/cocoa_window.m
@@ -990,8 +990,9 @@
 void _glfwSetWindowIconCocoa(_GLFWwindow* window,
                              int count, const GLFWimage* images)
 {
-    _glfwInputError(GLFW_FEATURE_UNAVAILABLE,
-                    "Cocoa: Regular windows do not have icons on macOS");
+    // Amethyst: regular windows have no icon on macOS. Do nothing and report nothing, as GLFW
+    // 3.3 did: Minecraft 1.13-1.18 treat any GLFW error during window creation as fatal, and
+    // they call glfwSetWindowIcon then.
 }

 void _glfwGetWindowPosCocoa(_GLFWwindow* window, int* xpos, int* ypos)
